# stdout:
Make the profile match its config: install addons in config that aren't
installed, and upgrade those whose newest release isn't the one installed.
Releases are compared by checksum, not by version.

With no addons named, it covers every addon in the profile. It never
changes config, and never uninstalls anything unless --prune is given.

Usage:
  knapsack update [addon...] [flags]

Examples:
  knapsack update
  knapsack update baganator-mirror
  knapsack update -A --prune

Flags:
  -A, --all-profiles     act on every profile
      --force            replace folders in AddOns that no addon owns
  -h, --help             help for update
  -p, --profile string   profile to act on (default $KNAPSACK_PROFILE, then the current profile)
      --prune            uninstall addons that are installed but no longer in config

Global Flags:
      --config string   use this config file instead of the default
  -v, --verbose         show progress and the underlying cause of errors
